 "content_notes": "Closed case: Faisal Shahzad pleaded guilty to all ten counts on 21 June 2010 and was sentenced to life in prison on 5 October 2010. There were no victims. The device, its contents and any explosion are never depicted: only smoke seeping from a parked SUV; the contents are one typed card. Shahzad is only an anonymous rim-lit silhouette (not a likeness, never a photo recreation), never posed heroically; none of his words or beliefs are quoted. The vendors, the mounted officer, the technician and the agents are generic figures with no insignia and no weapon; the real vendors and officers are not named on screen. The SUV is a generic dark SUV with no plate, badge or logo; the make is never said. No airline, dealer, website or police logo or wordmark is drawn: the billboards are abstract colour panels with no text and every card is our own typed graphic. The VIN is never shown (masked characters). No dialogue is invented. Legal status verified 2026-10-13.",
